extraction_notes: "WB13 Lone Star printed 40-41 (cache p041-p042, offset +1), every number read off 170 dpi renders. The entry points to the Dog Boy R.C.C. (printed 32-36) for its special powers, psionics, equipment and money; those were read from renders of printed 33-36 and restated here, so this class is self-contained and pairs with no race. || HEADING: the entry sits under Dog Boy Special Forces R.C.C.s and is headed Sea Dog R.C.C.; a racial class, so men_of_arms: false. || XP: the ladder headed Dog Boy (CS Soldier), Sea Dog (CS Navy) on the unnumbered page after printed 174 (cache p176), read off the render: 0, 1951, 3901, 8801, 17601, 25601, 35601, 50601, 70601, 95601, 125601, 175601, 225601, 275601, 325601 (level 15 ends at 375,000). || ATTRIBUTES (Newfoundland) as printed: I.Q. 3D6, M.E. 3D6+4, M.A. 3D6+6, P.S. 3D6+6, P.P. 3D6, P.E. 3D6+6, P.B. 3D6, Spd 3D6 running or swimming, 1D6 digging. The book says these are in addition to the Dog Boy''s Physical Bonuses (printed 33): +1D4 P.E., 1D4 P.S. (printed without the plus sign; read as a bonus) and +2D6 Spd, stored in bonuses.attributes. || POOLS: Hit Points 10 + P.E. + 1D6 per level. S.D.C. 30 plus those gained from physical skills: a racial figure that adds to what skills give, stored as bonuses.pools.sdc 30 and not as sdc_base, per the class-import rule for a racial S.D.C. P.P.E. 3D6. || PSIONICS (printed 33, items 4 and 5): effectively a master psionic; Sense Evil, Sense Magic, Sixth Sense and Empathy (receiver only) automatically, plus one Sensitive power of choice; I.S.P. is M.E. plus 1D6x10 (the cache reads !D6xlO), +10 per additional level. The save of 10 or higher belongs to the master tier and is in the ability text. || BONUSES (printed 33, items 5 and 6): +2 initiative, +1 strike, parry and dodge, +2 save vs disease, +2 vs possession, +1 vs psionic attack and +1 vs all forms of mind control. Half penalties when blind and the exhaustion rules are conditional and stored as ability text. || NATURAL ABILITIES: the Sea Dog''s own line (98% swim, hold breath 1D4+2 minutes, half damage from cold, water resistant fur, smell and tracking by scent -20%) plus the Dog Boy''s eleven numbered powers restated. Swimming 98% is also granted as the Swimming skill at a fixed 98 with no per-level gain. The -20% is recorded in the smell ability beside the printed Dog Boy percentages (70/54/40 become 50/34/20); the book does not say whether it also reaches tracking a supernatural being by psychic scent, and it was NOT applied there (judgement). Printed 33 reads Base Skill: 10% 44% per additional level under Recognize Psychic Scent, a misprint; stored as 10% +4% per additional level. Bite 1D6 nip and 2D6 full strength S.D.C. are the printed typical figures (printed 35); the book prints no Newfoundland bite. || SKILLS: American and Spanish at 90% as Language: Native Tongue 90 and Language: Spanish 90, no per-level gain. Basic Math is Mathematics: Basic 45+10 = 55. Radio: Basic 45+10 = 55. Read Sensory Equipment is Sensory Equipment 30+10 = 40. Paramedic 40+15 = 55. Pilot: Warships and Patrol Boats is Military: Warships & Patrol Boats 40+10 = 50. Pilot: Water Scooters is Water Scooters 50+10 = 60. Water Skiing & Surfing 40 and SCUBA 50 and Climbing 40 at catalog base (no bonus printed; the Dog Boy''s Climbing +10% is not repeated on the Sea Dog''s list). Advanced Fishing 30+10 = 40. Track & Hunt Sea Animals 35+10 = 45. Land Navigation 36+10 = 46. Wilderness Survival 30+10 = 40. W.P. Energy Pistol, W.P. Energy Rifle, one W.P. of choice. Hand to Hand: Expert, changed to Martial Arts for one other skill; no Assassin offered. || RELATED: five at level one, plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12, limits and bonuses as printed. Pilot is stored as the six catalog rows that match sail and motor boats, motorcycle, hovercycle, jet pack and truck. Medical, Rogue and Science: none. || SECONDARY: four at level one and two more at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12, same limits without the bonuses (the Dog Boy''s eight and levels 2, 4, 8, 12 are not the Sea Dog''s). || EQUIPMENT: Basically the same as the Dog Boy R.C.C. (printed 36), plus a wet suit and diving gear. Light (30 M.D.C.) or heavy (50 M.D.C.) Dog Pack DPM Riot armor is the single row dog-pack-dpm-riot-armor, whose text carries both; tinted goggles or a non-environmental helmet as a choice; PDD pocket audio recorder as pocket-digital-disc-recorder; 100 ft of lightweight rope as five lightweight-rope; 1D6 animal snares; a pair of vibro-knives or vibro-claws as a choice of two; C-14 Fire Breather or CP-40 as a choice; four E-clips. The vibro-saber or neuro-mace that many also have is not issued and is in the choice''s note. Diving gear is the catalog row scuba-gear (tank, regulator, mask and fins). Equipment Available Upon Assignment (grenades, flares, explosives, heavy weapons, optics, cameras, light vehicle, rations, non-regulation gear, full environmental DPM armor) is not starting equipment and is in GM Notes. || MONEY: Same as the Dog Boy R.C.C. but lives on a boat or a Navy base: a monthly salary of 200-300 credits (700 for officers) and player characters start with two months pay, so 400 to 600 credits. Stored as 600, the figure the dog-boy class carries for the same sentence; the book prints a range, not a roll. || NOT STORED AS MECHANICS: typical missions, tours of duty and maximum rank (printed 36) are the Dog Boy soldier''s and are summarised in GM Notes."
