## Lore

The Sea Dog is the Coalition Navy''s own Dog Boy, bred from the Newfoundland: a
big, web-footed working dog that has always been at home in cold water. The
mutant keeps the breed''s strength, stamina and steady temper, and adds hands,
speech and the psychic nose every Psi-Hound has for magic and the supernatural.

Sea Dogs crew patrol boats, dive, haul people out of the water, stand guard and
fight. Their sensing powers give a ship early warning of unnatural weather,
entities and things rising from below. The Coalition''s fleet is young and has
seen more of the Great Lakes and the Gulf of Mexico than of open ocean, so the
dogs are often the most comfortable sailors aboard, and their calm confidence
steadies the human crews they serve beside.

They are gentle and friendly by nature, eager to please, and quick to go to the
aid of any human in trouble. Nearly all Newfoundland mutants are made for the
Navy. One met outside the service is a runaway or the free born child of
runaways, and the Coalition treats both as enemies.

## GM Notes

The Sea Dog uses the standard Dog Boy powers with two changes: it swims at 98%
and shrugs off cold, and its nose is weaker (-20% to smell and tracking by
scent). The book does not say whether that penalty also applies to following a
supernatural being by its psychic scent; this entry leaves those rolls alone.

Pay is 200 to 300 credits a month (700 for an officer) with quarters, food,
clothing, medical care and equipment supplied; a Sea Dog lives aboard a boat or
on a Navy base. A player character starts with two months of pay.

Available on assignment rather than owned: hand and smoke grenades, 1D4 signal
flares, other explosives, heavy weapons, optical and camera gear, a light
vehicle, rations, and non-regulation weapons and armor for undercover work.
Full environmental Dog Boy armor goes to officers and special assignments.

Dog Boys rise no higher than Warrant Officer, few pass Sergeant Major, and none
ever command human troops. A deserter not caught within a week is usually left
alone unless he acts against the Coalition.

The optional size and breed tables are not used for this class. The Mutation
Abnormality Table is the G.M.''s call.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'sea-dog');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'sea-dog';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-sea-dog-class.sql');
